WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.755
Turn your reading into a short evaluation record.

2
00:00:03.755 --> 00:00:11.342
Name the configuration and commit, then record the derived parameters that matter to your workload.

3
00:00:11.342 --> 00:00:16.093
Add the platform, software versions and relevant test results.

4
00:00:16.093 --> 00:00:22.147
State the gaps, and choose one next experiment that would change your decision.

5
00:00:22.147 --> 00:00:32.876
For example, a controller project might first check interrupt behavior on its board; a Linux host might first establish a reproducible boot.

6
00:00:32.876 --> 00:00:35.251
Keep roadmap information dated.

7
00:00:35.251 --> 00:00:44.371
The July fifteenth, twenty twenty-six roadmap discusses CV64A60AX verification and dual-core lockstep integration work.

8
00:00:44.371 --> 00:00:54.180
Those entries help identify active engineering work, while completed capabilities still need release or implementation evidence.

